---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import SetupBuilder from "../components/SetupBuilder";
import ReleaseCards from "../components/ReleaseCards.astro";
import { currentReleasePair } from "../data/site";
---

<BaseLayout title="Install Certael — Core and optional Agent" description="Choose a game engine and follow the safe path to your first Certael-protected authoritative action.">
  <section class="page-hero shell">
    <p class="eyebrow">Get started</p>
    <h1>Protect the first action.<br /><span class="gradient-text">Keep the server in control.</span></h1>
    <p class="lede">Choose your engine and protection mode. Prebuilt packages require no native toolchain.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="section-tight shell"><SetupBuilder client:load /></section>
  <section class="section shell" id="compatibility">
    <div class="split-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">Current alpha pair</p><h2>Upgrade together.</h2></div><p>Core {currentReleasePair.core.tag} and Agent {currentReleasePair.agent.tag} share signed compatibility, build, protocol, and update contracts. Mixed older deployments are denied for new protected sessions.</p></div>
    <div class="prose-grid">
      <article class="prose-card"><h3>New installation</h3><ol><li>Install the Core package for your engine.</li><li>Deploy the authoritative server SDK and backend.</li><li>Generate and register a signed whole-build manifest for each exported build.</li><li>If the protected mode uses Agent, install its complete platform package and add the game with a signed per-game registration.</li><li>Bootstrap a fresh session and test replay, tampering, dishonest requests, manifest changes, deadline loss, and revocation.</li></ol></article>
      <article class="prose-card"><h3>Upgrading from older alphas</h3><ol><li>Stop protected matches and the old Agent.</li><li>Apply all Core database migrations through 016.</li><li>Deploy an offline-signed compatibility manifest and its public trust key.</li><li>Regenerate build manifests with SDK, engine adapter, ABI, protocol, and probe versions.</li><li>Deploy Core {currentReleasePair.core.tag}, install Agent {currentReleasePair.agent.tag}, and start fresh sessions.</li></ol></article>
    </div>
    <div class="callout"><strong>Do not copy one DLL over an older installation.</strong> Replace the complete engine package and use the Agent installer so its stable launcher, versioned binary, activation record, probe, and compatibility manifest stay together.</div>
    <div class="callout"><strong>What happens to old versions:</strong> supported versions start normally; deprecated versions start with an upgrade recommendation; required, revoked, unknown, or unverifiable combinations cannot start a new protected session. A verified Agent update is staged automatically and activates at relaunch.</div>
  </section>
  <section class="section shell" id="agent">
    <div class="split-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">Release channels</p><h2>Core first. Agent when needed.</h2></div><p>Core is required for the authoritative request path. Agent is a separately installed, optional user-mode companion for protected modes.</p></div>
    <ReleaseCards />
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
